@startuml expiration-guards
title Expiration-Kontrollpunkte: Cross-Device vs. DC API

state "Cross-Device (heute)" as CD {
  state "Verification angelegt\nexpiresAt = now + verificationTTL" as CD1
  state "GET /request-object\n**Guard 1** greift\nJAR exp startet JETZT" as CD2 #LightGreen
  state "GET /verifications/{id}\n**Guard 2** (Polling, wiederholt)" as CD3 #LightGreen
  state "POST response-data\n**Guard 3** (Claim)" as CD4 #LightGreen
  CD1 --> CD2 : Wallet scannt QR
  CD2 --> CD3 : Business Verifier pollt
  CD3 --> CD4 : Wallet antwortet
}

state "DC API Same-Device (neu)" as DC {
  state "Verification angelegt\nexpiresAt = now + verificationTTL\n**JAR exp startet BEREITS HIER**" as DC1 #Gold
  state "navigator.credentials.get()\nUser wählt Credential, Consent\n<i>Backend sieht nichts</i>" as DC2 #LightCoral
  state "POST dc-api/.../response-data\n**Guard 3** = einziger Kontrollpunkt" as DC3 #LightGreen
  DC1 --> DC2 : kein Backend-Kontakt
  DC2 --> DC3 : synchroner POST
}

note bottom of DC2
  **Blinde Phase.**
  Guard 1 entfällt (kein GET /request-object).
  Guard 2 entfällt (kein Polling).
  Nur der Cleanup-Scheduler (Guard 4)
  ist hier aktiv - und der *löscht*.
end note

@enduml